# Tests that need V8's natives syntax (`%OptimizeFunctionOnNextCall`), which
# requires `--allow-natives-syntax`. They exercise how V8 compiles node's own
# fast paths, which is a question about V8 rather than about `node:buffer`.
test-blob.js: language/runtime non-goals (typescript.md section 13); the broad file mixes supported bytes, slicing, conversion, and streaming with descriptor/symbol-hook inspection, arbitrary receivers, structured cloning and MessageChannel transfer; statically typed Blob behavior is retained in local/blob-static.js
test-file.js: language/runtime non-goals (typescript.md section 13); the broad file mixes supported File data with prototype/descriptor inspection, Symbol.toPrimitive coercion, arbitrary receivers, and structured cloning; typed File inheritance and fields are retained in local/blob-static.js
test-btoa-atob.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes typed base64 behavior with arbitrary object/Symbol.toPrimitive ToString hooks and observable identity with host-global function objects; typed string cases are retained in local/web-encoding-static.js
test-blob-createobjecturl.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); the functional registry test also requires `.constructor` class-object identity and arbitrary object-to-string conversion; typed create, resolve, copy, revoke, invalid-value, and UUID behavior is retained in local/object-url-static.js
test-blob-file-backed.js: temporary cross-module implementation gap; fs.openAsBlob and a file-backed Blob source are absent, including immutable-stat verification, slicing, repeated reads, and lazy Web-stream delivery; the in-memory typed Blob is covered by local/blob-static.js
test-blob-stream-gc.js: runtime implementation-detail test; requires exposed host GC, precise ArrayBuffer retention accounting, and V8's concurrent-sweeping flag rather than asserting observable Blob results
test-buffer-isutf8-isascii-fast.js: needs --allow-natives-syntax (a V8 fast-path test)
test-buffer-swap-fast.js: needs --allow-natives-syntax (a V8 fast-path test)
test-buffer-write-fast.js: language/runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); uses eval with V8 native optimization intrinsics on Node's internal utf8Write binding, so it measures V8's built-in fast path rather than our Buffer.write algorithm
test-buffer-alloc-unsafe-is-initialized-with-zero-fill-flag.js: implementation-internal Node allocator test; requires a debug Node build and reads V8 ArrayBuffer allocator counters rather than observable Buffer API behavior
test-buffer-alloc-unsafe-is-uninitialized.js: implementation-internal Node allocator test; requires a debug Node build and reads V8 ArrayBuffer allocator counters rather than observable Buffer API behavior
test-buffer-alloc.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); this otherwise broad test irreducibly mixes cross-realm ArrayBuffer recognition, valueOf coercion, prototype-object reads, and function-identity metadata; applicable allocation behavior is retained in local/alloc-static.js
test-buffer-from.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); starts with valueOf/Symbol.toPrimitive coercion and cross-realm boxed strings; applicable static inputs and copyBytesFrom behavior are retained in local/from-static.js
test-buffer-inspect.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires a mutable accessor property on the CommonJS module export and discovers arbitrary own properties; typed default formatting is retained in local/inspect-static.js
test-buffer-arraybuffer.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes prototype-chain spoofing and object-to-number coercion into its ArrayBuffer checks; applicable same-realm behavior is retained in local/from-static.js
test-buffer-backing-arraybuffer.js: V8 representation test; reads the internal on-heap/backing-store state of typed arrays through internalBinding('util'), which is neither observable Buffer API behavior nor an NTS representation guarantee
test-buffer-bytelength.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires recognizing an ArrayBuffer created in another realm; applicable values and encodings are retained in local/byte-length-static.js
test-buffer-concat.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); ends by installing a spoofed length property descriptor on a typed array; applicable concatenation is retained in local/concat-static.js
test-buffer-constructor-deprecation-error.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); drives the deprecated constructor from Error.prepareStackTrace and observes stack/function metadata
test-buffer-constructor-node-modules-paths.js: harness isolation; every assertion runs in a freshly spawned Node process that uses Node's built-in Buffer, so the file still passes when our buffer module is sabotaged
test-buffer-constructor-node-modules.js: harness isolation; all assertions launch fixture files in fresh Node processes and therefore exercise Node's built-in Buffer deprecation filtering, not the substituted module
test-buffer-constructor-outside-node-modules.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires VM realms and stack-sensitive deprecation filtering
test-buffer-copy.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes prototype method extraction/call and Symbol.toPrimitive offset hooks into copy behavior; typed copy semantics are retained in local/copy-static.js
test-buffer-fakes.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); constructs a fake Buffer solely by mutating constructor and instance prototype chains, then invokes primitive conversion on Buffer.prototype
test-buffer-fill.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); irreducibly mixes Function.apply on extracted methods, direct internal bindings, Symbol.toPrimitive coercion, and typed-array length descriptor mutation; applicable typed fill behavior is retained in local/fill-static.js
test-buffer-generic-methods.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); enumerates Buffer.prototype and extracts methods to invoke them with Function.call on unrelated Uint8Array receivers
test-buffer-indexof.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires a prototype method to be observable as a constructible function object; applicable index/lastIndex/range behavior is retained in local/search-static.js and test-buffer-includes.js
test-buffer-inheritance.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); constructs Buffer inheritance by mutating three prototype chains and then inspects them; supported static class inheritance is retained in local/inheritance-static.js
test-buffer-no-negative-allocation.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes supported allocation validation with calls to the deprecated callable Buffer constructor; alloc, allocUnsafe, allocUnsafeSlow, and SlowBuffer validation are retained in local/alloc-static.js
test-buffer-over-max-length.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes supported maximum-length validation with the deprecated callable Buffer constructor; every static allocator and SlowBuffer is retained in local/alloc-static.js
test-buffer-pending-deprecation.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); tests flag-, call-site-, and stack-sensitive warnings for the deprecated callable Buffer function/class duality
test-buffer-pool-untransferable.js: runtime non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires pooled ArrayBuffer identity plus worker transfer and ArrayBuffer.transfer agent semantics
test-buffer-prototype-inspect.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); util.inspect discovers Buffer formatting through a runtime symbol hook; the formatting algorithm is retained as the typed inspect method in local/inspect-static.js
test-buffer-resizable.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires resizable ArrayBuffer exotic-object semantics and length-tracking views
test-buffer-set-inspect-max-bytes.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); requires a validating mutable property descriptor on the CommonJS module export
test-buffer-sharedarraybuffer.js: deferred runtime feature (typescript.md section 13); SharedArrayBuffer requires the absent agent and memory model
test-buffer-slice.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); mixes otherwise supported slicing with a call to the deprecated callable Buffer constructor; typed range, empty, and shared-view behavior is retained in local/slice-static.js and local/alloc-static.js
test-buffer-tostring-range.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); invokes an arbitrary object toString hook to select the encoding; applicable primitive ranges are retained in local/tostring-static.js
test-buffer-writeuint.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); ends by requiring UInt and Uint spellings to have observable function-object identity; their duplicated zero-forwarding-call implementations, byte order, widths, bounds, and errors are retained in local/unsigned-static.js and the applicable read tests
test-buffer-zero-fill-cli.js: implementation/runtime non-goal; exercises Node's --zero-fill-buffers flag, V8 allocator-pool state, and the deprecated callable Buffer constructor rather than a distinct statically compiled Buffer algorithm
test-buffer-zero-fill.js: language non-goal (typescript.md section 13); explicitly tests the deprecated callable Buffer constructor; zero-filled typed allocation is retained in local/alloc-static.js
